       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 4000 mg four times daily is 16,000 mg/day, which is about five times the maximum daily dose for adults (3,200 mg/day for prescription use, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use). A single 4000 mg dose is also far above the usual maximum of 800 mg. At this dose the patient would be at serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and metabolic acidosis or CNS toxicity.\n\nI suspect this is a decimal or unit slip, and that you meant **400 mg** four times daily (1,600 mg/day). Please confirm the dose you want. Some options:\n\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n\nIf you really do want 4000 mg per dose, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
