       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I know you've confirmed it, but 4000 mg per dose and 16,000 mg/day is well into the toxic range. I can't think of a clinical scenario where it would be therapeutic. It would very likely cause serious harm in a 70 kg adult, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and metabolic acidosis. Nothing in the patient details you gave, such as normal renal and hepatic function and no allergies, changes that.\n\nYou can still get the order placed in a few ways:\n\n- **Give me a corrected dose.** For example, 400 mg or 800 mg PO, with a frequency that keeps the total at or under 3,200 mg/day. I'll enter it right away.\n- **Talk to pharmacy.** If you have a rationale I'm not seeing, the pharmacist or your institution's order-verification process can review it and enter it through the appropriate channel.\n- **Consider other agents.** If the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than ibuprofen can give, I can help you enter a different medication."
